@startuml Basic Prototype Pattern

' Define the styles
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam classFontStyle bold
skinparam classBackgroundColor #f8f9fa
skinparam classBorderColor #dee2e6
skinparam arrowColor #6c757d
skinparam stereotypeCBackgroundColor #e9ecef

' Title
title Basic Prototype Pattern - Core Structure

' Prototype Interface
interface Prototype <<interface>> {
  +clone(): Prototype
}

' Concrete Prototypes
class ConcretePrototypeA <<ConcretePrototype>> {
  -fieldA: String
  -fieldB: int
  +ConcretePrototypeA(fieldA: String, fieldB: int)
  +clone(): ConcretePrototypeA
  +setFieldA(fieldA: String): void
  +setFieldB(fieldB: int): void
}

class ConcretePrototypeB <<ConcretePrototype>> {
  -fieldX: String
  -fieldY: boolean
  +ConcretePrototypeB(fieldX: String, fieldY: boolean)
  +clone(): ConcretePrototypeB
  +setFieldX(fieldX: String): void
  +setFieldY(fieldY: boolean): void
}

' Client
class Client <<Client>> {
  -prototype: Prototype
  +Client(prototype: Prototype)
  +operation(): Prototype
}

' Prototype Registry (Optional)
class PrototypeRegistry <<Registry>> {
  -prototypes: Map<String, Prototype>
  +addPrototype(key: String, prototype: Prototype): void
  +getPrototype(key: String): Prototype
  +removePrototype(key: String): void
}

' Relationships
Prototype <|.. ConcretePrototypeA : implements
Prototype <|.. ConcretePrototypeB : implements
Client o--> "1" Prototype : uses
Client ..> Prototype : clones
PrototypeRegistry o--> "*" Prototype : stores

' Pattern component notes
note right of Prototype
  <b>Prototype Interface</b>
  Declares cloning method common
  to all prototypes.

  <b>Key Method:</b>
  clone() - creates copy of itself

  <b>Purpose:</b>
  • Provides common contract
  • Enables polymorphic cloning
  • Decouples client from concrete types
end note

note left of ConcretePrototypeA
  <b>Concrete Prototype</b>
  Implements clone() to create
  a copy of itself.

  <b>Clone Implementation:</b>
  • Create new instance
  • Copy all fields
  • Return the copy

  <b>Types of Cloning:</b>
  • <b>Shallow:</b> Copy field references
  • <b>Deep:</b> Clone referenced objects too
end note

note left of Client
  <b>Client</b>
  Creates new objects by
  cloning prototypes instead
  of using constructors.

  <b>Usage Pattern:</b>
  Prototype copy = prototype.clone();
  copy.setFieldA("modified");

  <b>Benefits:</b>
  • Don't need to know concrete class
  • Avoid complex initialization
  • Create variations easily
end note

note right of PrototypeRegistry
  <b>Prototype Registry (Optional)</b>
  Central repository for managing
  commonly used prototypes.

  <b>Purpose:</b>
  • Store pre-configured prototypes
  • Retrieve by name/key
  • Avoid recreating same prototypes

  <b>Usage:</b>
  registry.addPrototype("standard", proto);
  Prototype p = registry.getPrototype("standard");
  Prototype copy = p.clone();
end note

' Legend
note right of Prototype
  <b>Prototype Pattern Components:</b>

  <b>Prototype:</b> Interface declaring clone()
  method for creating copies of objects.

  <b>ConcretePrototype:</b> Implements clone()
  to return a copy of itself. Contains logic
  for copying all fields.

  <b>Client:</b> Creates new objects by asking
  prototype to clone itself, rather than
  calling constructors directly.

  <b>Registry (Optional):</b> Manages a catalog
  of frequently used prototypes, allowing
  retrieval and cloning by identifier.

  <b>Key Benefits:</b>
  • Avoid complex object construction
  • Hide concrete classes from client
  • Add/remove prototypes at runtime
  • Reduce subclassing
  • Clone objects without coupling to class

  <b>Intent:</b>
  Specify the kinds of objects to create
  using a prototypical instance, and create
  new objects by copying this prototype.

  <b>When to Use:</b>
  • Object creation is expensive
  • Many similar objects needed
  • Avoid complex initialization
  • Reduce number of classes
end note


@enduml